# Release battery evidence

Issue 91 reproduces a clean stage despite a failed process, missing required
tests, or failures labelled as a historical baseline. The replacement keeps
baseline attribution but never treats a failing baseline as complete evidence.

Required behavior:

- Retain process exit, signal and spawn-error facts separately from test
  verdicts. A failed process cannot pass through successful-looking counters.
- Read machine evidence. Missing, malformed, contradictory, partial or skipped
  required test evidence prevents a passing battery. Human-readable output is
  retained for diagnosis, not used to manufacture missing machine evidence.
- Discover the local test inventory from the actual checkout and split Node
  and Vitest suites by their imports. Execute each selected file once and
  reconcile the reported files with that inventory. Explicit benchmark probes
  remain a separately named diagnostic surface, not hidden skipped tests.
- Require the API-key capture preflight with independently supplied
  expectations before the full battery starts. Missing admission evidence
  refuses the full run before allocating expensive test stages. Local unit
  commands remain available without this acceptance preflight.
- Preserve source identity, exact selected/excluded inventory, checker hashes,
  raw reports and process logs. A scoped marker/admission check never claims
  that the test battery ran.
- Require clean, unchanged Git revision/status observations before a battery
  can qualify its commit. Dirty source refuses the full battery before test
  stages; standalone local tests remain separate. Passing assertions alone
  cannot produce a committed-source battery verdict.
- Keep inventory classification and script suffixes explicit and shared. A new
  undeclared test surface fails both gate checking and runner admission.

This is a local release battery. Passing it does not establish the complete
four-category/runtime/backend matrix, native reference qualification,
migration, privacy, recovery or measurement. Those acceptance requirements
remain active under decision 0013. A corrected checker itself still needs an
independent adversarial pass before its verdict supports a release claim.

The independent review of the first correction confirms the original false
passes are fixed and identifies source qualification, inventory provenance and
classification gaps. Its raw fixture/report evidence remains preserved under
the reviewer's registered output; the follow-up correction must receive its
own frozen review. The installed Vitest 5.0.1 reporter does not emit optional
interruption/runtime-error/open-handle fields. Those optional guards apply only
when supplied; process termination and missing reports provide the observed
interruption check for that installed reporter.
